{
  "rule": "fv3_absolute_vorticity_cellmean",
  "applicable": false,
  "skip_reason": "Layer-A canonical drive of `fv3_absolute_vorticity_cellmean` requires ESS `discretize` to dispatch (a) a cubed_sphere multi-axis selector at cell_center for the relative-vorticity row, and (b) the `kind: \"constant\"` self-targeting source-row selector that contributes the Coriolis term f = 2·Omega_rot·sin(lat) without an operand read. Both pieces sit behind ESS extensions that hold the other cubed_sphere FV rules' Layer-A back today: the multi-axis selector is the same blocker as `covariant_laplacian_cubed_sphere` / `transport_2d`, and `kind: \"constant\"` is the new selector kind introduced for source terms with closed-form coefficients evaluated against per-cell metric bindings (here `lat` at CellCenter and the scalar `Omega_rot`). Once both ESS extensions land, this stub can be promoted to a hand-pinned canonical contract that pins ω_abs = ω_rel + 2·Omega_rot·sin(lat) bit-for-bit against the imperative reference on a small cN cubed sphere with non-trivial latitude variation across panels.",
  "reference_implementation": {
    "module": "EarthSciDiscretizations",
    "function": "fv_absolute_vorticity",
    "path": "src/operators/vorticity.jl",
    "comment": "Imperative reference for absolute vorticity ω_abs = ω_rel + f, where f = 2·Omega_rot·sin(lat). Composes with `fv_vorticity_cellmean`. Default Omega_rot = 7.292e-5 rad/s for Earth. Follows Harris et al. (2021) §6.3."
  },
